Notice

OpenFF is an independent, non-commercial project published for study,
preservation and interoperability: it lets people play and modify the copies
of Final Fantasy III and Final Fantasy IV (the 3D remakes) that they own. It is
not affiliated with, endorsed by or connected to Square Enix Co., Ltd. Final
Fantasy and the games' names, characters, art, music and data are their
owners' trademarks and copyrighted works.

No game asset, data file or executable of the games is contained in this
repository or its releases. Running OpenFF requires the Steam releases of the
games, legitimately obtained and installed on the same machine; OpenFF reads
them in place and writes nothing into them without a backup. The code under
OpenFF/GlobalScope recreates the games' program logic through reverse
engineering of the publicly sold releases so that they can run on modern
systems and be modified; it is provided as-is, for educational and
interoperability purposes.

The MIT licence above covers the code and documentation written for OpenFF.
It grants no rights in the games themselves. Anyone redistributing OpenFF, a
build of it or a mod made with it is responsible for complying with the laws
of their jurisdiction and with the games' own terms; the authors and
contributors accept no liability for how the software is used.
